### F.2 Anomaly Detection Models

The anomaly detection models in Table [IX](https://ar5iv.labs.arxiv.org/html/2602.16738#A6.T9 "Table IX ‣ F.2 Anomaly Detection Models ‣ Appendix F Training Configuration Details ‣ Self-Evolving Multi-Agent Network for Industrial IoT Predictive Maintenance") were configured to balance detection sensitivity with computational efficiency in a streaming setting. Isolation Forest and One-Class SVM serve as unsupervised baselines that operate directly on the ISAPCA-reduced feature space, providing robust detection without labeled anomalies. The sequence models (LSTM and Transformer) capture temporal dependencies in sensor trajectories, enabling early detection of gradual degradations rather than only abrupt faults. Hyperparameters were selected through preliminary grid search to maintain stable training, avoid overfitting, and keep inference latency compatible with real-time IIoT deployment.

